"Love in This Club" debuted at number eighty-three on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], on the issue dated March 1, 2008.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2008-03-01/hot-100?order=gainer |title=Hot 100 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]] |date=March 1, 2008 |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> The next week it moved to number fifty-one, due to high [[airplay]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/1046411/flo-rida-starts-tenth-week-atop-hot-100 |title=Flo Rida Starts Tenth Week Atop Hot 100 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Nielsen Company|Nielsen Business Media]] |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> The song continued to receive many [[spin (radio)|spins]], and in its third week it reached the top of the Hot 100, gaining the 'Airplay Gainer' honor the same week. Replacing "[[Low (Flo Rida song)|Low]]" by [[Flo Rida]] and [[T-Pain]], "Love in This Club" also sold 198,000 [[music download|downloads]] in that week.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/1046342/ushers-club-rockets-50-spots-to-top-hot-100 |title=Usher's 'Club' Rockets 50 Spots To Top Hot 100 |first1=Silvio |last1=Pietroluongo |first2=Anthony |last2=Colombo |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Nielsen Company|Nielsen Business Media]] |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> On April 5, 2008, the song was again named the 'Airplay Gainer', however it was shifted from the number-one spot by [[Leona Lewis]]' "[[Bleeding Love]]", having spent three weeks atop the chart.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2008-04-05/hot-100 |title=Hot 100 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]] |date=April 5, 2008 |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> It fell off on June 7, having spent twelve weeks in the top ten.<ref name="Usherhot100"/>

On the [[Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs]], the song first appeared on February 23, 2008, at number fifty-one making it the highest debut of the week.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2008-02-23/r-b-hip-hop-songs?order=gainer |title=R&B/Hip-Hop Songs |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]] |date=February 23, 2008 |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> On April 12, it replaced [[Keyshia Cole]]'s "[[I Remember (Keyshia Cole song)|I Remember]]" at number one.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2008-04-12/r-b-hip-hop-songs |title=R&B/Hip-Hop Songs |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]] |date=April 12, 2008 |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> After four weeks "Love in This Club" was moved from the top spot by [[Lil Wayne]]'s "[[Lollipop (Lil Wayne song)|Lollipop]]".<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2008-05-10/r-b-hip-hop-songs |title=R&B/Hip-Hop Songs |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]] |date=May 10, 2008 |access-date=November 25, 2010}}</ref> The song also reached number four on the [[Pop 100]],<ref name="allcharts">{{AllMusic|class=artist|id=p44890|tab=charts-awards/billboard-singles|access-date=April 24, 2011|label=Usher}}</ref> and has been [[RIAA certification|certified platinum]] by the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA). On the year-end charts for 2008, it was ranked number eight on the Hot 100,<ref name="2008Hot100"/> number fifteen on the Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs and number thirteen on the Pop 100.<ref name="2008rnb"/><ref name="2008pop"/> It was also ranked number eighty-five on the 2000s' Hot 100 list,<ref name="2000sHot100"/> and number ninety-nine on the decade-end Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs.<ref name="2000srnb"/> As of August 1, 2010, "Love in This Club" has sold 2,453,000 units, according to [[Nielsen Soundscan]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://new.music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart_watch/59953/week-ending-aug-1-2010-the-downloading-of-eminem/ |title=The Downloading Of Eminem |first=Paul |last=Grein |publisher=[[Yahoo! Music]] |date=August 4, 2010 |access-date=December 9, 2010}}</ref>

Internationally, the song reached the top ten of numerous singles charts. It reached number six on the [[Canadian Hot 100]],<ref name="canada"/> number four on the [[UK Singles Chart]],<ref name="ukchart">Peak chart positions for albums, singles and other charted songs in the United Kingdom:
* {{cite web|url=http://www.officialcharts.com/artist/_/usher/|title=Usher Chart History|publisher=[[Official Charts Company]]|access-date=August 15, 2010}}
* "Can U Get wit It" and "There Goes My Baby": {{cite web|url=http://www.zobbel.de/cluk/CLUK_U.HTM|title=Chart Log UK: U2 – Utopia|publisher=Zobbel|access-date=February 6, 2010}}
* "U Don't Have to Call": {{cite web|url=http://www.zobbel.de/cluk/CLUK_P.HTM|title=Rodney P. – The Pussycat Dolls|publisher=Zobbel|access-date=September 18, 2013}}
* "Lil Freak": {{cite web|url=http://zobbel.de/cluk/100619cluk.txt|title=Chart Log UK: New Entries Update|access-date=October 2, 2010|publisher=Zobbel}}
* "Hot Tottie": {{cite web|url=http://www.zobbel.de/cluk/101002cluk.txt|title=Chart Log UK: New Entries Update|access-date=October 2, 2010|publisher=Zobbel}}
* "Dirty Dancer": {{cite web|url=http://www.officialcharts.com/artist/_/Enrique%20Iglesias/|title=Enrique Iglesias Chart History|publisher=Official Charts Company|access-date=August 15, 2010}}
* "Lemme See": {{cite web|url=http://www.theofficialcharts.com/singles-chart/|title=Official UK Singles Top 100 - 23rd June 2012 - Official Charts|publisher=Official Charts Company|archive-url=https://www.webcitation.org/68UgRGerI?url=http://www.officialcharts.com/singles-chart/|archive-date=June 17, 2012|access-date=November 5, 2017|url-status=live}}
* "What's a Man to Do": {{cite web|url=http://www.zobbel.de/cluk/CLUK_U.HTM|title=Chart Log UK: U2 – Utopia|publisher=Zobbel|access-date=February 6, 2010}}
* "First Dance": {{cite web|url=http://zobbel.de/cluk/100403cluk.txt|title=Chart Log UK: New Entries Update|publisher=Zobbel|access-date=January 12, 2011}}</ref> number eight on the [[ARIA Charts|Australian ARIA Singles Chart]],<ref name="australia"/> number three on the [[Irish Singles Chart]],<ref name="ireland"/> and number five on the [[Japan Hot 100]],<ref name="japan">{{cite web|title=Chart Track|url=http://www.oricon.co.jp/rank/ja/w/2008-06-09/}}</ref> and was certified silver by the [[British Phonographic Industry]] (BPI) and 2× Platinum by the [[Australian Recording Industry Association]] (ARIA). Having been certified gold by the [[Recording Industry Association of New Zealand]], it also topped the [[New Zealand Singles Chart]], replacing "[[No Air]]" by [[Jordin Sparks]] and [[Chris Brown (American singer)|Chris Brown]] on May 5, 2008.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://rianz.org.nz/rianz/chart.asp?chartNum=1615&chartKind=S |title=Top 40 singles (#1615) |publisher=[[Recording Industry Association of New Zealand]] |date=May 5, 2008 |access-date=November 26, 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120602122944/http://rianz.org.nz/rianz/chart.asp?chartNum=1615&chartKind=S |archive-date=June 2, 2012 }}</ref> After one week it was removed by Brown's "[[Forever (Chris Brown song)|Forever]]",<ref>{{cite web|url=http://rianz.org.nz/rianz/chart.asp?chartNum=1616&chartKind=S |title=Top 40 singles (#1616) |publisher=[[Recording Industry Association of New Zealand]] |date=May 12, 2008 |access-date=November 26, 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120602122947/http://rianz.org.nz/rianz/chart.asp?chartNum=1616&chartKind=S |archive-date=June 2, 2012 }}</ref> and was certified platinum on June 1, 2008.
The single also found chart success in Europe, reaching number three on the [[European Hot 100 Singles]]. In individual countries, "Love in This Club" attained top-ten places in [[Ultratop 50|Flanders]],<ref name="flanders"/> [[SNEP|France]],<ref name="france"/> [[Media Control Charts|Germany]],<ref name="germany"/> [[VG-lista|Norway]],<ref name="norway"/> [[IFPI|Slovakia]],<ref name="slovakia">{{cite web |url=http://www.ifpicr.cz/hitparadask/index.php?a=titul&hitparada=18&titul=144828&sec=eee8e42f9f586e367127996528e712b8 |language=sk|title=RADIO TOP100 Oficiálna|publisher=IFPI|access-date=February 13, 2008}}</ref> [[Sverigetopplistan|Sweden]]<ref name="sweden"/> and [[Media Control Charts|Switzerland]].<ref name="switzerland"/> It also appeared on the singles charts of [[Ö3 Austria Top 75|Austria]],<ref name="austria"/> [[Ultratop 50|Wallonia]],<ref name="wallonia"/> [[IFPI|Czech Republic]],<ref name="czech"/> [[Tracklisten|Denmark]],<ref name="denmark"/> [[Finland's Official List|Finland]],<ref name="finland"/> [[Mahasz|Hungary]],<ref name="hungary"/> and [[Mega Single Top 100|the Netherlands]].<ref name="netherlands"/> In 2008, "Love in This Club" sold 5.6&nbsp;million digital downloads worldwide.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ifpi.org/content/library/DMR2009.pdf |title=Digital Music Report 2009 |publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry]] |year=2009 |access-date=October 24, 2013 |archive-date=September 24, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150924033145/http://www.ifpi.org/content/library/DMR2009.pdf |url-status=dead }}</ref>

